WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:34.833
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna spoke </b>
<b>about the wise and the ignorant.</b>

2
00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:39.625
<b>He explained that although their actions </b>
<b>and processes may be the same,</b>

3
00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:44.583
<b>the one who is wise, the learned one,</b>
<b>does not worry about the fruits,</b>

4
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:47.166
<b>does not keep attachment to the results.</b>

5
00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:49.291
<b>They simply perform their duty,</b>

6
00:00:49.291 --> 00:00:56.000
<b>and their purpose is the welfare of society</b>
<b>and to guide others on the right path.</b>

7
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.625
<b>But in such a case, how can the</b>
<b> wise guide the path of others?</b>

8
00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:08.125
<b>How can the ignorance of those attached to </b>
<b>the fruits of action be dispelled?</b>

9
00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:15.083
<b>Lord Krishna says here</b>

10
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:16.541
<b>that a learned person</b>

11
00:01:16.541 --> 00:01:21.666
<b>does not stop those who are attached to the fruits </b>
<b>of action from performing their duties,</b>

12
00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:25.333
<b>nor does he disturb their minds</b>

13
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:29.583
<b>by saying that they are doing something wrong</b>
<b>by being attached to the fruits.</b>

14
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:33.208
<b>Rather, he makes himself an example.</b>

15
00:01:33.208 --> 00:01:39.708
<b>By living a life of non-attachment, </b>
<b>he inspires others towards such a life.</b>

16
00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:44.250
<b>But if renunciation of attachment is the right path,</b>

17
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:51.125
<b>then shouldn't a spiritually accomplished person </b>
<b>impart this knowledge to others?</b>

18
00:01:51.125 --> 00:01:57.250
<b>In such a case, wouldn't it be right to</b>
<b>discourage them from a life of attachment?</b>

19
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.166
<b>No!</b>

20
00:01:58.166 --> 00:02:00.166
<b>This would not be right.</b>

21
00:02:00.166 --> 00:02:02.625
<b>Understand this practically.</b>

22
00:02:02.625 --> 00:02:05.916
<b>Giving up attachments is not so simple;</b>

23
00:02:05.916 --> 00:02:09.291
<b>it is a process that takes time.</b>

24
00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:16.000
<b>Even those who have become wise have attained </b>
<b>freedom from attachment to the fruits step bystep.</b>

25
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.625
<b>Such a big change will not come</b>
<b>just by someone saying so,</b>

26
00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:25.500
<b>and one who is truly learned knows this.</b>

27
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.750
<b>The renunciation of attachments </b>
<b>will happen voluntarily.</b>

28
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:33.791
<b>For this, it is necessary that a person reaches </b>
<b>that level of knowledge</b>

29
00:02:33.791 --> 00:02:36.958
<b>where this becomes directly evident to them.</b>

30
00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:39.958
<b>If, before reaching that level of knowledge,</b>

31
00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:45.083
<b>a person is untimely encouraged</b>
<b>to give up attachments,</b>

32
00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:47.750
<b>it can prove detrimental.</b>

33
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:53.875
<b>Untimely imparted knowledge can create </b>
<b>doubt in that person's mind.</b>

34
00:02:53.875 --> 00:02:58.625
<b>And this doubt is like a hole in a boat.</b>

35
00:02:58.625 --> 00:03:00.250
<b>Even if slowly,</b>

36
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.750
<b>earlier that boat was able </b>
<b>to float and cross the river,</b>

37
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:12.500
<b>but now if the hole of doubt appears </b>
<b>in that boat, it will surely sink.</b>

38
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.166
<b>It is possible that due to this doubt,</b>

39
00:03:15.166 --> 00:03:17.958
<b>In order to give up attachments,</b>

40
00:03:17.958 --> 00:03:20.666
<b>that person may consider it appropriate </b>
<b>to abandon action altogether.</b>

41
00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:23.541
<b>It is possible that they may become inactive.</b>

42
00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:28.333
<b>Someone has rightly said that </b>
<b>an idle mind is the devil's workshop.</b>

43
00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:32.708
<b>Inactivity is even more </b>
<b>harmful than selfish action.</b>

44
00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:38.333
<b>Therefore, it is necessary that a knowledgeable </b>
<b>person does not give such verbal advice.</b>

45
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:40.708
<b>Rather, by making oneself an example,</b>

46
00:03:40.708 --> 00:03:43.833
<b>through one's own actions, one's own conduct,</b>

47
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:49.000
<b>and the extraordinary life transformation</b>
<b>resulting from it, one should inspire others,</b>

48
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.416
<b>attract them towards such a life.</b>

49
00:03:52.416 --> 00:03:55.166
<b>It is extremely important to remember this,</b>

50
00:03:55.166 --> 00:03:58.875
<b>because this is where people </b>
<b>often make mistakes.</b>

51
00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:02.416
<b>Renouncing attachment does </b>
<b>not mean renouncing action.</b>

52
00:04:02.416 --> 00:04:05.708
<b>You will have to save yourself from inactivity</b>

53
00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:08.875
<b>and also save others from it.</b>

54
00:04:08.875 --> 00:04:10.208
<b>Remember,</b>

55
00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:14.125
<b>Lord Krishna Himself is also a proponent of action.</b>

56
00:04:14.125 --> 00:04:19.291
<b>He too is performing His duty in </b>
<b>this battle of Mahabharata.</b>

57
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:26.875
<b>This verse is saying that</b>

58
00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:29.875
<b>those who are wise, who are learned,</b>

59
00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:36.583
<b>should not eradicate ignorance</b>
<b>by scolding or criticizing it.</b>

60
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:42.375
<b>To dispel ignorance, the learned must </b>
<b>become an example themselves,</b>

61
00:04:42.375 --> 00:04:45.625
<b>so that others can be inspired.</b>

62
00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:48.375
<b>Why so?</b>

63
00:04:48.375 --> 00:04:50.250
<b>Consider,</b>

64
00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:55.916
<b>was the one who is wise today always wise?</b>

65
00:04:55.916 --> 00:04:57.208
<b>No, right?</b>

66
00:04:57.208 --> 00:05:04.791
<b>They too acquired knowledge over time, </b>
<b>and they should not forget this.</b>

67
00:05:04.791 --> 00:05:08.750
<b>And knowledge also says</b>

68
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:15.541
<b>that people understand practical examples </b>
<b>more than verbal instructions.</b>

69
00:05:15.541 --> 00:05:19.541
<b>Apply this to your personal life as well.</b>

70
00:05:19.541 --> 00:05:25.666
<b>It is possible that many people </b>
<b>may come before you in life</b>

71
00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:33.250
<b>who are not as mature as</b>
<b>you in skills, emotions, or spirituality.</b>

72
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.583
<b>For example, let's assume</b>

73
00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:43.208
<b>that a friend of yours gets stressed </b>
<b>out quickly in situations.</b>

74
00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:45.541
<b>But you are not like that.</b>

75
00:05:45.541 --> 00:05:51.208
<b>You have made yourself so strong </b>
<b>through meditation and practice</b>

76
00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:57.000
<b>that you handle such situations </b>
<b>with great calmness.</b>

77
00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.666
<b>Now think,</b>

78
00:05:59.666 --> 00:06:05.083
<b>would it be right for you to be </b>
<b>disappointed by that friend's nature,</b>

79
00:06:05.083 --> 00:06:12.083
<b>to be angry with them, or </b>
<b>if you just tell them to be calm,</b>

80
00:06:12.083 --> 00:06:16.291
<b>will they become calm?</b>

81
00:06:16.291 --> 00:06:17.791
<b>No, right?</b>

82
00:06:17.791 --> 00:06:20.500
<b>When a person is under stress,</b>

83
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:27.041
<b>neither scolding nor instructions</b>
<b>to be calm work at that time.</b>

84
00:06:27.041 --> 00:06:33.583
<b>Yes, if you really want to help, </b>
<b>then help by your example.</b>

85
00:06:33.583 --> 00:06:35.416
<b>Let them calm down,</b>

86
00:06:35.416 --> 00:06:42.958
<b>then suggest the remedies </b>
<b>that you yourself use to fight stress –</b>

87
00:06:42.958 --> 00:06:46.375
<b>closing your eyes and taking deep breaths,</b>

88
00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:50.000
<b>going for a walk somewhere for a while, etc.</b>

89
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.166
<b>Also,</b>

90
00:06:51.166 --> 00:06:54.750
<b>you can give them examples from your life,</b>

91
00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:58.416
<b>when you too were in some terrible dilemma,</b>

92
00:06:58.416 --> 00:07:04.250
<b>and how slowly, by thinking, </b>
<b>you came out of that dilemma,</b>

93
00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:09.791
<b>what was your thought process </b>
<b>to solve the problem.</b>

94
00:07:09.791 --> 00:07:11.083
<b>By doing so,</b>

95
00:07:11.083 --> 00:07:14.583
<b>you are not trying to prove them wrong,</b>

96
00:07:14.583 --> 00:07:15.791
<b>but</b>

97
00:07:15.791 --> 00:07:22.000
<b>you are simply sharing the </b>
<b>examples that helped you.</b>

98
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:28.333
<b>This will make them understand that </b>
<b>experiencing stress is not abnormal.</b>

99
00:07:28.333 --> 00:07:31.666
<b>They will also know that</b>

100
00:07:31.666 --> 00:07:37.541
<b>problems can be solved with a </b>
<b>positive thought process.</b>

101
00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:38.750
<b>Remember,</b>

102
00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.666
<b>conquer ignorance not by criticism,</b>

103
00:07:41.666 --> 00:07:42.708
<b>but</b>

104
00:07:42.708 --> 00:07:46.541
<b>by personal examples.</b>

105
00:07:50.916 --> 00:07:52.083
<b>In a family,</b>

106
00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:54.458
<b>among relatives,</b>

107
00:07:54.458 --> 00:07:58.375
<b>everyone has their own skills.</b>

108
00:07:58.375 --> 00:08:01.000
<b>But this also means that</b>

109
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:06.833
<b>someone may definitely be weak in some work.</b>

110
00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:08.458
<b>For example,</b>

111
00:08:08.458 --> 00:08:15.791
<b>assume that you yourself are very skilled</b>
<b>in music and musical instruments.</b>

112
00:08:15.791 --> 00:08:20.125
<b>In such a situation, you went to </b>
<b>a relative's or friend's house,</b>

113
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:25.458
<b>and they have newly learned to</b>
<b>play a musical instrument.</b>

114
00:08:25.458 --> 00:08:27.750
<b>They are very excited about this</b>

115
00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:32.666
<b>and present this new interest of theirs before you.</b>

116
00:08:32.666 --> 00:08:34.875
<b>They are new,</b>

117
00:08:34.875 --> 00:08:38.166
<b>not as skilled as you.</b>

118
00:08:38.166 --> 00:08:45.875
<b>As a result, you see many flaws in their music.</b>

119
00:08:45.875 --> 00:08:49.375
<b>Would it be right to criticize?</b>

120
00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:52.666
<b>Will it help them?</b>

121
00:08:52.666 --> 00:08:56.708
<b>Won't they be discouraged by the criticism?</b>

122
00:08:56.708 --> 00:09:00.083
<b>If you are truly their well-wisher,</b>

123
00:09:00.083 --> 00:09:05.208
<b>you will surely want to help them.</b>

124
00:09:05.208 --> 00:09:06.416
<b>In such a case,</b>

125
00:09:06.416 --> 00:09:10.833
<b>another way can also be adopted.</b>

126
00:09:10.833 --> 00:09:12.833
<b>The way of praise –</b>

127
00:09:12.833 --> 00:09:21.208
<b>praise of their enthusiasm, praise of </b>
<b>the parts of the music that were good.</b>

128
00:09:21.208 --> 00:09:26.875
<b>Now how to help in increasing their skills?</b>

129
00:09:26.875 --> 00:09:29.333
<b>By accompanying them.</b>

130
00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:35.916
<b>You can teach them a few things by </b>
<b>playing the same musical instrument your way.</b>

131
00:09:35.916 --> 00:09:40.166
<b>You can also give them the example of the time</b>

132
00:09:40.166 --> 00:09:43.291
<b>when you yourself were new in this field.</b>

133
00:09:43.291 --> 00:09:48.583
<b>When you too made mistakes, how you learned.</b>

134
00:09:48.583 --> 00:09:50.083
<b> Praise,</b>

135
00:09:50.083 --> 00:09:54.125
<b>and then personal example.</b>

136
00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:59.541
<b>This will keep them encouraged and</b>
<b>they will also learn from you.</b>

137
00:09:59.541 --> 00:10:00.708
<b>Also,</b>

138
00:10:00.708 --> 00:10:04.666
<b>not only will their interest and skill increase,</b>

139
00:10:04.666 --> 00:10:09.125
<b>but their affection for you will also increase.</b>

140
00:10:09.125 --> 00:10:11.125
<b>Think,</b>

141
00:10:11.125 --> 00:10:19.041
<b>you can use this process of praise and </b>
<b>personal example in many situations.</b>

142
00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.750
<b>In a professional environment, </b>
<b>there are many types of people,</b>

143
00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.708
<b>everyone's level of skill is different.</b>

144
00:10:30.708 --> 00:10:32.125
<b>Imagine that</b>

145
00:10:32.125 --> 00:10:39.208
<b>you are working with a colleague</b>
<b>who is not mature in work efficiency,</b>

146
00:10:39.208 --> 00:10:41.666
<b>who is new.</b>

147
00:10:41.666 --> 00:10:44.541
<b>Now in such a situation, would it be right</b>

148
00:10:44.541 --> 00:10:47.541
<b>to lower the expectations from them?</b>

149
00:10:47.541 --> 00:10:54.041
<b>Or would it be right to constantly put pressure </b>
<b>on them to increase their work level?</b>

150
00:10:54.041 --> 00:10:57.416
<b> If the level of expectation is lowered,</b>

151
00:10:57.416 --> 00:11:02.125
<b>they will never learn, </b>
<b>their progress will not happen.</b>

152
00:11:02.125 --> 00:11:06.791
<b>On the other hand, if too much pressure is created,</b>
<b>they will be discouraged.</b>

153
00:11:06.791 --> 00:11:09.875
<b>The right path is between these two.</b>

154
00:11:09.875 --> 00:11:14.125
<b>High work standards will have </b>
<b>to be expected from them,</b>

155
00:11:14.125 --> 00:11:16.000
<b>so that they develop,</b>

156
00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.750
<b>but this work will have to be done </b>
<b>not just by putting pressure,</b>

157
00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:24.250
<b>but by helping them, by teaching them.</b>

158
00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.208
<b>This will increase their skills,</b>

159
00:11:26.208 --> 00:11:30.958
<b>and also, because of getting help, </b>
<b>they will remain enthusiastic.</b>

160
00:11:30.958 --> 00:11:36.625
<b>The core idea here is that everyone </b>
<b>has the ability to raise their level,</b>

161
00:11:36.625 --> 00:11:41.875
<b>if needed, only encouragement </b>
<b>and guidance are required.</b>

162
00:11:41.875 --> 00:11:44.708
<b>Contempt and criticism, unnecessary pressure,</b>

163
00:11:44.708 --> 00:11:47.166
<b>these measures never work.</b>

164
00:11:47.166 --> 00:11:49.166
<b>Understand this.</b>

165
00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:51.125
<b>Adopt positive measures,</b>

166
00:11:51.125 --> 00:11:53.916
<b>expect high work standards from others,</b>

167
00:11:53.916 --> 00:11:59.583
<b>and then prove by your help that it is possible.</b>

168
00:11:59.583 --> 00:12:00.541
<b>Also,</b>

169
00:12:00.541 --> 00:12:06.375
<b>this process of helping them</b>
<b>can be beneficial for you as well.</b>

170
00:12:06.375 --> 00:12:08.458
<b>Everyone has their own perspective.</b>

171
00:12:08.458 --> 00:12:10.583
<b>It is possible</b>

172
00:12:10.583 --> 00:12:13.583
<b>that while helping your colleague,</b>

173
00:12:13.583 --> 00:12:16.208
<b>you may also come across an opportunity</b>

174
00:12:16.208 --> 00:12:20.333
<b>that shows you a new perspective on a problem.</b>

175
00:12:20.333 --> 00:12:21.708
<b>Remember,</b>

176
00:12:21.708 --> 00:12:25.416
<b>when you help someone, </b>
<b>when you teach someone,</b>

177
00:12:25.416 --> 00:12:28.583
<b>you yourself also learn a lot.</b>

178
00:12:28.583 --> 00:12:34.250
<b>Such a positive environment of help is </b>
<b>so beneficial not only for your colleague</b>

179
00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:35.250
<b>but</b>

180
00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:40.791
<b>also for you and the organization as well.</b>

181
00:12:40.791 --> 00:12:45.791
<b>An environment where not only </b>
<b>the quality of work will increase</b>

182
00:12:45.791 --> 00:12:49.666
<b>but professional relationships will also be sweet.</b>

183
00:12:49.666 --> 00:12:51.166
<b>Think about it.</b>

